## Topics

`aeo /` entity clarity, structured data completeness, extractable tables, question
and answer coverage, specification table design.
`geo /` citation panel method, assistant citation patterns, source corroboration and
third party mentions, generative answer surfaces, citation rate measurement, getting
a product recommended by an assistant.

## Look for

A measurement method over a tactic list. The citation panel is the metric: a fixed set
of 40 to 60 real category questions, run weekly, recording whether the brand is named
and which source got cited instead. Those cited sources are the work queue.

Named practitioners who show what changed their citation rate are the strongest
sources here.

## Skip

**"What is GEO" explainers.** Definitional content is exactly what a frontier model
already knows, so it fails the discard test.
**Beginner AEO tutorials** for the same reason.
Confident tactical claims with no measurement behind them. This field is new and most
of what is written about it is guessing dressed as certainty.

## The artifact that serves 3 jobs

A complete, correct, machine-readable specification table with units answers the
sizing objection on the page, is what an answer surface extracts, and is what a
generated answer cites.

## Expect to revisit

Thin and contested. Tier honestly, set short review dates, re-verify this folder every
6 months.

## Scope mix

Mostly growth. The one near-baseline: the specification table.

